## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is exercised, achieving line coverage, but almost nothing is actually *asserted*. Bugs would sail through these tests undetected.

---

### 🔴 Critical — No Meaningful Assertions (9 of 10 tests)

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | What Could Break Undetected |
|---|------|--------------|-----------------------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17-21) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assert at all | `Save` could silently no-op; product never persisted |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L32-35) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assert | Price could remain unchanged or be set to 0 |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38-42) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assert | Product could still exist after "deletion" |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L63-66) | **Dead variable** — result never checked | Count could return -1, int.MaxValue, anything |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68-74) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assert | Discount could multiply instead of subtract, or corrupt all prices |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85-88) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assert | Parsing could silently drop records or mangle fields |
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L24-29) | **Weak assert** — `IsNotNull` only | Returns wrong SKU, wrong name, wrong price? Test still passes |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L45-52) | **Weak assert** — `IsNotNull` only | Could return both products, zero products, or wrong products |
| 9 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L77-82) | **Weak assert** — `IsNotNull` only | CSV could be malformed, empty string, or have wrong delimiters |
| 10 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L55-60) | **Weak assert** — `IsNotNull` only | Could return empty list despite having added a product |

---

### Concrete Fixes

```csharp
// 1. AddProduct — verify round-trip
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_PersistsProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(product, retrieved);
}

// 2. UpdatePrice — verify new price AND unchanged fields
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_UpdatesOnlyPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", updated.Name); // regression guard
